WEBVTT

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.770
Boo!

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.320
<i>No, help!</i>

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.280
<i>Please, don't kill me.</i>

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.460
That clock I borrowed from Miya

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.210
makes waking up so stressful.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.470
Today I will not forget to buy
new batteries for my clock.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.900
Tell me, tell me, what color is in season now?

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.150
Smiling white

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.610
Tearful blue

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.240
Let's mix them together and find out

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:04.580
Today is sunny, so take out your canvas

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.330
Have some ice cream and lemon soda

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.000
Then draw some exciting and colorful toppings

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.010
Hey, rough sketch, please

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:19.930
Let's do a self portrait contest

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.310
Yuno

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:27.190
All right! Don't get grouchy later

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.930
Miyako

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.440
Hiro

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:34.280
When the switch is flipped, I go wa-ha-ha

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.690
Sae

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:40.620
I hope everyone is having a great time

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.160
The race is on

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.950
I've gotta finish my apple quickly

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.540
No, that's not for eating

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.210
Let's take it easy

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.170
Fruits are our display models

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.010
So start drawing

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.890
It's our homework

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.270
September 4th

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.270
The Wolf of the Shinjuku Backstreets

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.610
Good morning, Miya.
You got up early this morning.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.240
Morning.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.610
What's wrong?

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:23.620
For some reason, I woke up in the
middle of non-REM sleep.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.410
Okay, I'll pull myself together,
and say, ''Good morning.''

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.290
Huh?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.460
What's this?

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.170
Wow, a lot of lottery tickets!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.590
A sign of a crime.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.390
A crime?

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.100
In other words, a lottery ticket
kidnapping case.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.890
When it comes to lottery tickets,
I think you say ''theft.''

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.270
How about bribing a lottery ticket?

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:57.280
You don't bribe lottery tickets.
You bribe someone with lottery tickets.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.610
Then, how about lottery ticket murder?

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.240
A lottery ticket isn't a person.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.950
He must have dropped it.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.120
Oh, so this is a lottery ticket
lost and found case.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.290
Excuse me.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.130
Did you drop this?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.750
Huh?

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.260
It's gone.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.970
Here you go.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.880
Thank you, I owe you one.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.260
Good thing, you got it back.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.930
Here you go.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.270
This is for the Big Dream Lottery.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.020
The first prize is 300 million yen cash.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.150
He gave us 10% of what we found.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.780
The early bird catches 300 million yen.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.280
Only if you win.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.910
But 300 million isn't my thing.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.660
Eight zeros are way too big of a number.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:57.170
True, you only see this kind of number in math
or statistics in the social study class.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.720
The Cafe's curry is 300 yen,
so you can eat one million servings.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.260
Suppose you eat curry for three meals a day...

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:09.640
...333,333 days.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:14.520
That equals to 913 years.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.480
It can feed you for nine generations.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.610
The school cafe's curry rice everyday...

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.360
My entire body would turn yellow.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.160
What would people in India say?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.830
But what if we won 300 million yen?

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.080
I would...

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.130
...build a fountain or
a swimming pool back home.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.340
Or a maze of trees.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.840
Oh, but the yard in my home isn't that big.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:47.220
What would you do, Miya?

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.560
First, I'll take my ID and family seal
to pick up the money.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.230
It's risky to carry cash,
so I'll open a bank account right away.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.940
But I must hedge the risk of the payoff,

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.190
How do you know so much?
so I'll deposit only 10 million yen, and the rest
should be split to as many banks as possible.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.940
so I'll deposit only 10 million yen, and the rest
should be split to as many banks as possible.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.240
Hey, the drawing day is today.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.870
You're right.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.120
Hey, over here!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.710
Indeed, it is fall.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.540
Principal, watch out!

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.470
Sports

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.470
Fall is the best season for sports.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:33.930
Ms. Yoshinoya said something about a
special class. I wonder what it is?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.270
Beats me.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.850
Hello!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.940
Well, let's begin a special class.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.400
Please come in.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.030
Excuse me.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.240
Oh no, are you wondering who the person is?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:55.580
Perhaps a substitute teacher
while I take maternity leave?

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.080
That means you're assuming that I have

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.460
engaged in things with a man that
will give me a baby!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.170
Is that what you are thinking?
That's sexual harassment!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.930
You're the sexual harasser!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:20.480
Maiko Kishi

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.770
She's my former student, so she's an
upperclassman of all of you.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.680
Her name is Kishi.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.440
She paid a visit, so I dragged her to my class.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.780
Hello, I'm Maiko Kishi.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.610
She used to be called Maimai.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:33.330
After I graduated from Yamabuki,
I went to an art college.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:37.830
She was an excellent student,
so she was admitted by recommendation.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.670
My major is oil painting.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.460
She also worked part-time as a
product campaign girl.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.630
Right now, I'm working on a film.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:53.300
I winded up talking to you in the class.
Anyway, nice to meet everyone.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:03.560
Well, I think it's easier to see what I've done.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.490
I created this to enter a contest.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.490
Mai, how are you doing?

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.700
Mai, we're doing all right.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.870
Are you eating well?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.370
Wrong one!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:17.410
If things get tough,
you can come home any time.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.790
No, not this one.
If things get tough,
you can come home any time.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.540
If things get tough,
you can come home any time.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.830
Honey, you'll make Mai feel obligated.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.750
What the? Why...
But you know...

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:27.840
Mai!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.630
Oh no!
Mai!

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.890
Sorry about that.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.510
Fight for it, Kishi.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.600
Let's see...

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.560
Oh good.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.560
The spring wind blows a romantic
miracle into the city.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.100
This is a promo for a short film
I made for a contest.
The spring wind blows a romantic
miracle into the city.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.400
This is a promo for a short film
I made for a contest.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.350
This is a promo for a short film
I made for a contest.
A sudden encounter. Fate brings two together.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.730
A sudden encounter. Fate brings two together.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.980
My dream is to become a film director.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.150
My dream is to become a film director.
Distant memories, fragile dreams
and finite time...

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.070
So, I've been making films since
my second year in college.
Distant memories, fragile dreams
and finite time...

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:54.820
Their feelings overcome all things...

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:56.370
A dream...
Their feelings overcome all things...

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.910
Their feelings overcome all things...

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.540
To me, filming is like...

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:04.040
Kind of like a lover.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.670
What?!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.880
Did you break up with Shimada?

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:13.430
Oh please, that was in high school.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.260
Excuse me. I have a question.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.600
Ask away.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:21.350
Why did you decide to make movies,
instead of drawing?

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:28.110
Well, let's see, when I entered high school,

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.780
I just liked painting a little more
than the others did.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:36.530
I didn't have any clear goals or
dreams for the future.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:43.120
I happened to become a cameraman for the
class play during the cultural festival.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.620
Screenplay

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.460
That got me hooked on filming.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:54.510
Just like painting, you can capture
important moments in life,

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.720
or even create one by making movies.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:03.310
When I realized it, the world through
the viewfinder looked bright.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.980
Before I knew it, I was completely into it.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.810
Bright...

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:13.400
By the way, everyone from the class
unanimously wanted me to take a part.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.740
So, I was the lead in the class play.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.120
What?

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:24.450
Well, the play was a parody
of Princess Kaguya.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.330
That makes perfect sense.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.290
Art Room

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.380
Art

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.380
Fall is the best season for art.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:41.260
Well, looks like we still have time.
Any ideas?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.520
You can do whatever you want, Kishi.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:46.560
Well, let's see...

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.900
How about telling me your dreams?

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.690
Now then...

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.320
You first.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.030
I want to become an art teacher.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.030
A wonderful dream. What about you?

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.660
I want to be an illustrator.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.620
Sounds good. What about you in the back?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.290
Tell us.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.290
Um...

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:12.960
My dream...

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:19.720
My dream is about me chasing a bowl of rice,
with cod roe in my hand.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.510
But the rice keeps pulling away from me,
and I can't catch it.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.220
Music Room

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.900
Solo Singing

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.230
Fall is the best season for solo singing?

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.440
Reading

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:40.280
All right, that will end today's special class.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.490
Thank you very much.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.530
Thank you.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.660
Yunocchi, let's go eat.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.290
Okay...

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.790
What's wrong?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:55.380
Sorry, Miya. Can you wait just a bit?

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.300
Good luck! Even love-at-first-sight can grow.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.550
Don't worry about the obstacles
of being the same gender!

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.350
That's not it!

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.560
Ms. Kishi?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.680
Umm, I...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.100
What's the matter?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:17.940
I don't have a clear goal.
Do you think I'll find a dream like you?

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.570
Let's see...

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:26.990
At your age, everything you see
can be your inspiration.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:34.250
Once you realize that, I think you can
find important things in your life.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.500
I see.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.760
A touching story, isn't it?

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.090
Don't be so emotional, teacher.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.470
I didn't know there was a former
student like her.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.600
She'll be a movie director in the future.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.600
Oh, that's right.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:52.850
There they are.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.560
Here, take them.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.190
What for?

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.360
Lottery tickets?

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:01.320
We got them as a gift.
We have four, so you can have one.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.280
The early bird will catch lottery tickets.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:05.910
Are you sure?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.330
Thanks.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.830
Today is the drawing day.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.000
If you win 300 million yen, what would you do?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.040
I guess I'll save.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.170
Then think thoroughly about what to do with it.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.010
I will...

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.470
...renovate the Hidamari Apartments.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.850
You sound very mature.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:33.350
I'll go all out and make it artsy,
like Sagrada Familia.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.810
That's an off-the-scale dream.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.980
Hiro, that's just impossible.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.860
Right, not just the money, but time...

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:46.700
That's not it!
Blocking the sun will be a serious problem.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.320
That's so down-to-earth.

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:57.000
I guess the drawing hasn't been done yet.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.750
Come on. Mine is 87926375.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.340
Yes, come in.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.180
Yuno, thanks for earlier.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.930
We bought some munchies near the train
station. Would you like some?

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.010
Here it comes!

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:13.180
I'll make some tea then.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:18.020
That painting... It's not yours is it?

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.020
Oh, it's...

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.410
Phew, that was heavy.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:32.080
The art club doesn't have very many boys,
so taking out trash is really tough.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.460
Looks like all kinds of stuff was tossed out.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.290
Amazing...

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.250
What?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.170
I can still use this.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.470
These will be picked up in the evening.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.220
So if there's anything you want,
take it before then.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.470
Okay, thank you.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.850
All right, let's find some treasure.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:58.480
Miya, this stuff is trash. I don't think
you'll find anything valuable.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.570
Is this...

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.740
<i>Dad, hang in there. Dad! Dad!</i>

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:12.030
When it comes to munchies,
takoyaki is the best.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:15.950
Really? I think it's usually something sweet.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.920
That's a beautiful brassica napus.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:22.790
Last time I heard that name was when
I was still in grade school.

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.340
Anyway, it's really a nice piece of art,

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.970
and I didn't want it to go to waste,
so I brought it home.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.930
That's done by a student in
the class next to ours.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.850
Really? Do you know that person?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.180
Yeah... What was her name?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.770
Anyway, her skills are well known
among the juniors.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.360
I see.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.980
But...

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.450
I think she left the school recently.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:56.290
I don't know the details, but she transferred
out because of family circumstances.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.620
Oh no!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.250
That's why she threw away her sketchbook.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.630
Yuno...

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:08.380
She got into Yamabuki High,
and she's so talented,

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.180
but she had to quit in the middle.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:17.810
I'm not even good, and have no talent,
but got into Yamabuki.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:22.150
I don't even have my own dream.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.520
Yuno, don't be so hard on yourself.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:30.490
Right, we don't know if she
transferred against her wish.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.820
Cut the gloom, Yunocchi!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.040
When you have tasty munchies,
you can't ruin the mood.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.660
Miya, that hurt.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.510
When it comes to munchies,
cream puffs are the best.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.010
Miyako, didn't you say takoyaki earlier?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.640
Hey, where did you get that hammock?

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.770
I bought it at a garage sale a while ago.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.350
It was a bit expensive, but
it's a treat to myself.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.940
I thought I could use it as a bed.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.900
A hammock instead of a bed?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.400
It will get cooler.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:15.280
Without the mat, it will be colder
than sleeping on the floor.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.950
Exercise gear!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.580
Wow!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.330
A draft net.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.960
Wow!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.590
If I do this, it's cat's cradle!

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.170
Wow!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.680
Goodnight!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:39.430
If you put it down on the floor,
it's not a hammock any more.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.390
Let me out. I'm innocent!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.020
Enough already!

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.570
When it comes to munchies, jello is the best.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:56.700
Are these the diet jelly that didn't work?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:01.040
It still tastes good,
and the calories are almost zero.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.500
An inventory clearance, huh?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:07.580
Come to think, what happened to
the lottery drawing?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:13.010
Well, we've been watching TV for quite a while,
but it hasn't come up yet.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.800
I wonder if it's already over?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.760
In any case, the evening news
should pick up the story.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:22.930
If we just want to know the numbers,
the evening newspaper would be better.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:28.190
You're right, sometimes the TV screen
changes before we can get it down.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:31.610
How is your lottery luck usually?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.400
Pretty good.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:38.610
A while ago, I won a year's worth
each of chikuwa,

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:43.120
kamaboko and naruto at a
local shopping arcade.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.750
Your luck all goes to minced
and steamed fish meat.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:51.630
I won 10,000 yen cash three times.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:57.510
That's amazing, my highest prize was
1 ,000 yen. Oh, but a while ago...

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:01.800
I won an autograph in a
manga magazine's sweepstakes.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.850
Ume Aoki

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:06.350
I'm jealous. I've been unlucky.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:11.900
I even got excluded from a
free prize for everyone.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.440
How could that possibly happen?!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:15.900
From Chika

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.200
Hold on a second.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.030
Hello...

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.160
What are you talking about?
That's impossible, of course.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.000
No, no matter what.

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:32.040
I got the evening paper.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:33.880
Yay!

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:39.630
Let's see... Where is it?

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.550
There it is!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.680
Okay, I'll start from the lowest prize.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.140
The seventh prize ends with 5.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.730
The sixth prize ends with 42.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:52.980
The fifth prize ends with 592.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:56.190
The fourth prize ends with 52331.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.320
The third prize ends with 244953.
How are we doing?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.410
Terrible.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.030
Yours didn't win either?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.870
Okay, the last two prizes.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:11.170
The second prize is 89336122,
and the first prize is 19640627.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.670
Oh, it's the same.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.380
What?!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:20.760
I noticed that the first prize number is
the same as my mom's birthday.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.640
That's so misleading.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.180
Looks like we didn't win.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.560
But it was thrilling and fun.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.730
The early bird didn't get anything.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.860
What are you looking at?

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:41.990
Here, look.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:49.290
''The 28th Blue Sky Foods Film Contest...
Special Prize: Maiko Kishi''

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.250
You mean the same Kishi person
you two were talking about?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.540
Wow, that's great.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:55.920
What?

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:56.750
What's wrong?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.920
The title of the movie is
''The Wolf of the Shinjuku Backstreets.''

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.550
The what?!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:08.430
I owe you. I ran out of my shampoo.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.220
She's amazing.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:15.270
Kishi is working hard to reach her goals.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.900
Hardwork will not betray you.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.740
Say, can I sleep at your place tonight?

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.410
Sure...

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:38.750
Hey, Miya, do you think a person's
dream can be taken away?

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.800
Are you talking about the
artist of the brassica napus?

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:44.090
That too, but...

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:48.890
Can a dream be taken away because
of reasons you can't control,

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:55.190
even if you work hard like Kishi?

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.020
I don't think so.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:02.360
Unless you say, ''I quit,'' it always
stays right there in your heart.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:08.200
So, as long as the brassica napus
person hasn't given up,

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.950
she should still be chasing her dream.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.960
Maybe she threw away her sketchbook after
discovering something she truly wanted to do,

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.500
just like Kishi did.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:22.170
Yeah, probably so.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:30.510
She must be working hard somewhere
out there to chase her dream.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:37.350
I asked Kishi if I'll be able to find my dream.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.020
Your dream won't go anywhere.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.820
Your dream must be waiting for
you to find it somewhere.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:48.530
Thank you.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.950
Time to sleep?

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:52.580
Yup, goodnight.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.200
Goodnight.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.370
Oh no! I have to set the alarm clock.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:00.880
Oh snap, I forgot to buy the batteries.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:04.670
That means, tomorrow morning,
the alarm will go...

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:08.550
End of September 4th
To Be Continued

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:08.550
<i>Help!</i>

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:21.360
It eventually fades into the tall sky

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.980
The voices

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.780
Bubble up and fade away

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:31.200
Fade away

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.910
They return to where they belong

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:44.420
And fuse together as they sparkle and collide

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:49.880
This body feels like one entity

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:53.050
Yet, it's made of infinity

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:56.430
Caught a falling drop of water

00:22:56.430 --> 00:23:02.440
And now I'm taking a closer look

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:05.110
Awakening Drive

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:09.530
Dash into the sky in our bare feet

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:13.740
Close your eyes, can you see it?

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:16.910
It's a rainbow bridge, let's run toward it

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.620
Awakening Drive

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:22.960
A dazzling spark will break a star into pieces

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:31.130
Scattering across the sky and falling,
now in my hands

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:37.890
I have a piece of a dream, shining so bright

00:23:37.900 --> 00:24:00.170
Next Episode

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:43.700
Listen guys, the principal
is being mean to me!

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:47.790
Please Ms. Yoshinoya, don't cry.
You're making me want to cry.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:51.080
What's wrong, Yuno? You're acting strange.

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:55.090
It's a special day, so everyone shows
a different side from normal.

00:23:55.090 --> 00:23:57.880
I'm starving. Let's go eat lunch! Lunch!

00:23:58.340 --> 00:24:02.300
Next Episode is
''November 3rd: Her Highness Yuno''

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:06.850
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High,
so please, join us again.
